<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kunming</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kunming is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a> province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the northern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-dian">Lake Dian</a>. The lands around the lake were the heartland of the ancient Dian kingdom, and the city grew as a regional centre under the Nanzhao and Dali kingdoms and later Chinese dynasties. In 1662 the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-ming">Southern Ming</a> ruler, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongli-emperor">Yongli Emperor</a>, was executed there, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-sangui">Wu Sangui</a> afterwards governed Yunnan from the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kunming.jpg" alt="Kunming" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 瑞丽江的河水 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%BA%94%E5%8D%8E%E5%8C%BA%E5%A4%A9%E9%99%85%E7%BA%BF_-_%E8%88%AA%E6%8B%8D_-_2025-05-16_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
